WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
Let's make An autumn leaf garland.

2
00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:05.900
Clip dry leaves onto a short string in a repeating pattern.

3
00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:10.245
An adult displays the garland indoors, beyond children’s reach.

4
00:00:10.625 --> 00:00:12.705
Make this project with a grown-up.

5
00:00:13.085 --> 00:00:15.815
Gather the supplies listed below the video.

6
00:00:16.195 --> 00:00:18.440
Pause whenever you need more time.

7
00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:22.150
An adult manages the string and display location.

8
00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:28.536
Keep the garland away from beds, necks, heaters, flames and active play; no outdoor

9
00:00:28.536 --> 00:00:28.965
hanging.

10
00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:31.690
Step 1.

11
00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:33.350
Sort the colours.

12
00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:35.995
Lay six leaves on the table.

13
00:00:36.375 --> 00:00:41.860
Choose a repeating order, such as gold, orange, red, then gold, orange, red.

14
00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:45.555
Check that each leaf has a firm stem or strong base.

15
00:00:45.935 --> 00:00:47.315
Grown-up help.

16
00:00:47.695 --> 00:00:50.895
Check leaves and remove brittle or unsuitable pieces.

17
00:00:52.333 --> 00:00:53.513
Step 2.

18
00:00:53.893 --> 00:00:55.288
Lay out the string.

19
00:00:55.668 --> 00:00:59.103
Place the 60 centimetres string straight on the table.

20
00:00:59.483 --> 00:01:01.898
Leave 10 centimetres clear at each end.

21
00:01:02.278 --> 00:01:06.848
Lay the six leaves along the middle with roughly 7 centimetres between them.

22
00:01:07.228 --> 00:01:08.608
Grown-up help.

23
00:01:08.988 --> 00:01:11.228
Handle and supervise the string.

24
00:01:12.667 --> 00:01:14.012
Step 3.

25
00:01:14.392 --> 00:01:15.962
Clip the first leaf.

26
00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:18.582
Fold a leaf stem over the string.

27
00:01:18.962 --> 00:01:23.347
Slide a large paper clip over the folded stem so it holds both stem

28
00:01:23.347 --> 00:01:24.287
and string together.

29
00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:28.132
If the stem snaps, clip the broad leaf base instead.

30
00:01:28.512 --> 00:01:29.892
Grown-up help.

31
00:01:30.272 --> 00:01:32.947
Help with firm clips and fragile stems.

32
00:01:34.334 --> 00:01:35.484
Step 4.

33
00:01:35.864 --> 00:01:37.429
Repeat the pattern.

34
00:01:37.809 --> 00:01:40.754
Clip the remaining five leaves in the chosen order.

35
00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:42.979
Keep the garland lying flat.

36
00:01:43.359 --> 00:01:48.361
Gently slide the clips to balance the spaces, then check each leaf stays in

37
00:01:48.361 --> 00:01:48.719
place.

38
00:01:49.099 --> 00:01:50.479
Grown-up help.

39
00:01:50.859 --> 00:01:53.234
Inspect clips and loose pieces.

40
00:01:54.667 --> 00:01:55.842
Step 5.

41
00:01:56.222 --> 00:01:57.812
Display with an adult.

42
00:01:58.192 --> 00:02:03.050
An adult tapes both string ends to a suitable indoor display point beyond children’s

43
00:02:03.050 --> 00:02:03.397
reach.

44
00:02:03.777 --> 00:02:06.912
Use a shallow curve with no long dangling ends.

45
00:02:07.292 --> 00:02:10.027
Take it down if leaves begin to crumble.

46
00:02:10.407 --> 00:02:11.787
Grown-up help.

47
00:02:12.167 --> 00:02:16.617
Choose the location, attach both ends and remove it after display.

48
00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.915
Here are three ideas for your finished project.

49
00:02:21.295 --> 00:02:24.845
These example pictures were made with artificial intelligence.

50
00:02:25.225 --> 00:02:27.245
Your creation can look different.

51
00:02:27.625 --> 00:02:31.185
Remove clips and string for reuse, then sort the leaves.

52
00:02:31.565 --> 00:02:35.260
Display temporarily indoors and check for crumbling leaves.

53
00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:36.630
Well done.

54
00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:39.440
Take a moment to enjoy what you made.

